  "reviewedBoundaries": [
    {
      "area": "AppOwner clock ownership",
      "sourceSites": [
        "Modules/Services/SelfRenewal/SelfRenewalAppOwner.swift:55",
        "Modules/Services/SelfRenewal/SelfRenewalAppOwner.swift:73"
      ],
      "conclusion": "Both existing constructors pass the same injected clock to their existing handoff and Session. Handoff uses that clock for its actual save receipt; Journal validates createdAt <= capturedAt <= updatedAt. Existing AppExecution/Automatic positive methods now assert capturedAt equals fixture date. No alternate data owner, reader lifetime workaround or Journal validation relaxation."
    },
    {
      "area": "Disabled automatic observation",
      "sourceSites": [
        "Modules/Services/SelfRenewal/SelfRenewalAppOwner.swift:224",
        "Modules/Services/SelfRenewal/SelfRenewalAppSession.swift:521"
      ],
      "conclusion": "Session observation is nonoptional and supplies disabled when policy absent. Bootstrap refreshes it after both success/failure. New explicit-false early return is after task/foreground guards and before clearing bootstrap problem; enabled and uninitialized paths retain original worker flow. Actual foreground material/storage assertions stay strict."
    },
    {
      "area": "Glyph transform",
      "conclusion": "Real native nonnil midpoint caret must remain in first-glyph closed insertion interval 0...1 and the transformed view must return that identical value. Pixel equality, exact geometry translation/size and outside hit rejection remain."
    },
    {
      "area": "Actual provider request body",
      "conclusion": "Only test URLProtocol captures the actual stream if httpBody absent; reads at most 64KiB and propagates stream/budget failures. Original exact provider POST endpoint/body and forbidden Apple credential/header assertions are unchanged."
    },
    {
      "area": "Actual source replacement failure",
      "conclusion": "Test now unwraps the real Coordinator.Interrupted -> authenticated Client.OperationFailure -> BookSourcePersistenceFailure.writeFailed(.replace,_) chain seen in the d820 failure. Requires upload stage, remote creation, attempted verified cleanup with no cleanup errors, durable uploadIntent, exact uploaded bytes, zero Upgrade and original blocked target directory."
    },
    {
      "area": "Authenticated cancellation",
      "conclusion": "No broad error acceptance: requires session-stage OperationFailure, no remote creation/possible Upgrade, underlying Swift CancellationError or Transport.Failure.cancelled only, empty upload and zero Upgrade. execute wraps errors inside openSession at stage session. Raw prior cast nil alone does not prove which permitted underlying form next SDK will expose."
    },
    {
      "area": "Owned-application observation refusal",
      "conclusion": "Prior real submit must have exactly one Lookup and Upgrade. Rejected owned-root configuration must not increase either count and must retain exact Journal bytes and nil access. This retains current-process evidence rejection rather than treating an owned fixture as installed application proof."
    },
    {
      "area": "Archive aggregate budget",
      "conclusion": "2MiB compressed placeholder for each 256MiB declaration passes the existing 200x+64KiB ratio and entry limit. First two sum to 512MiB; third exceeds aggregate limit before ratio evaluation. Original independent ratio, oversized archive/entry/count/directory and CRC/compression negative vectors remain."
    }
